    "updated_at": "2022-12-12T01:17:36Z",
    "body": "To what extent is it helpful to be explicit about things? When thinking about a step like this, I tend to think of something like:\r\n\r\n\r\n  5. If _qualifiedName_ contains a U+003A (:), then run the following steps:\r\n    1.  Let _splitResult_ be the result of [strictly split](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#strictly-split) given _qualifiedName_ and U+003A (:).\r\n    2. Set _prefix_ to _splitResult_[0].\r\n    3. Set _localName_ to _splitResult_[1].\r\n\r\nUnwrapping things like this feels a bit verbose. Is there a better way?",
